\section*{Product-CM intersections of Hodge-generic curves in A2}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 016; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that a Hodge-generic curve in $\mathcal A_2$ over algebraic numbers meets the locus of surfaces isogenous to an elliptic product with a CM factor only finitely often.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 016; 2026-09-24), canonical product isogenies and degeneration comparisons bound heights along the curve. Period estimates produce a Galois-orbit lower bound, which conflicts with the definable counting bound unless only finitely many such points occur.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 016; 2026-09-24).

\subsection{Formal verification}
